	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Not all battles are face to face, particularly in situations where such a conflict would be decidedly one-sided. No, in truth there are many excellent reasons to engage in asymmetric warfare, and the Guerilla is a master of the ins and outs of doing so.</p><p>Trained warriors who travel in small squads through hidden paths to ambush, outflank, and outmaneuver larger and more cumbersome enemies in the hinterlands, guerillas often present themselves as freedom fighters and are often regarded as terrorists. In truth, they are warriors. Soldiers of a different brand of combat who give and follow orders like anyone else.</p><p><strong>Table: Guerilla</strong></p><table style=\"width: 100%; height: 134.4px;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 6.69216%;\"><col style=\"width: 93.1166%;\"></colgroup><thead><tr style=\"text-align: center; height: 16.8px;\"><td style=\"height: 16.8px;\">Level</td><td style=\"height: 16.8px;\">Features</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr style=\"text-align: center; height: 16.8px;\"><td style=\"height: 16.8px;\">3rd</td><td style=\"height: 16.8px;\">@UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-class-features.Item.gcTSnYQI3Xa9JcU6]{Ambush Warfare} @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-class-features.Item.V8GMWA1gzQqSj7fR]{Guerilla Leader}</td></tr><tr style=\"text-align: center; height: 33.6px;\"><td style=\"height: 33.6px;\">7th</td><td style=\"height: 33.6px;\">@UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-class-features.Item.E06s0XvH0qJeXXAd]{Commando}</td></tr><tr style=\"text-align: center; height: 33.6px;\"><td style=\"height: 33.6px;\">11th</td><td style=\"height: 33.6px;\">@UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-class-features.Item.V0awCe2baGc9Pr6R]{Wiley Combatant}</td></tr><tr style=\"text-align: center; height: 33.6px;\"><td style=\"height: 33.6px;\">15th</td><td style=\"height: 33.6px;\">@UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-class-features.Item.FTKjtGZfCwycHup7]{Freedom Fighter}</td></tr></tbody></table>",
